  "limitations": [
    "Training data is 2002-2005 email (SpamAssassin corpus). Modern spam/phishing styles, languages and obfuscation techniques are under-represented, so real-world performance will be lower than test metrics.",
    "Ham comes largely from technical mailing lists and newsletters received by a few people; business, personal and non-English mail is under-represented, which raises false-positive risk on such mail.",
    "Test metrics come from the same corpus (random group-aware split), not from a later time period or a different organisation; they are optimistic estimates of deployment performance.",
    "Header text is intentionally excluded from TF-IDF to avoid learning collection artefacts; only a few header properties are used. Pasting a body without headers disables those header signals.",
    "No sender reputation, authentication (SPF/DKIM/DMARC), URL reputation or attachment scanning is performed.",
    "Explanations are per-feature contributions in score space (log-odds/margin); they describe the model, not ground truth, and character n-gram signals can be hard to interpret.",
    "Educational project: not a substitute for a production mail-security gateway.",
    "These structured features never vary in the training data, so the model cannot use them even though they are extracted and displayed: missing_date."
